# deml-ui — Cursor rules (design system SoT LOCKED)

This repo is the DEML design system — **single source of truth** for the
**new-from-the-start / atelier** look consumed by deml and Django static chrome.

## Do

- Change visuals in `components/<name>/` and `styles/tokens.css` / `styles/base.css`.
- Keep an 8px grid (`--grid` / `--space-*`), dual `data-theme`, equal tile gaps
  (`--tile-gap`), identical row heights (`--tile-row-unit`), and locked chart
  aspect (`--chart-aspect: 2.4`).
- Use tokens only for chrome — `--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--tile-*`, `--chart-*`,
  `--font-*`, `--tracking-*`, `--hit-target`.
- Large bold display + letterspaced secondary / eyebrows; preserve type recipes in `base.css`.
- Run `npm run sync` after adding/removing component folders; `npm run build` before release.
- Prefer WCAG 2.0 AA patterns already used in base + headless primitives
  (focus-visible, contrast, hit targets, reduced motion).

## Do not

- Reintroduce Viking-UI naming, void-black / electric `#2176ff` suite chrome, or `--viking-*` tokens.
- Hand-edit generated wrappers under `src/angular/markup/` or `generated/` — regenerate via sync.
- Break the chart aspect contract or invent one-off spacing outside the token scale.
- Ship arbitrary hex in component CSS for chrome outside the atelier token set.

Consumer guidance for the Angular app lives in deml `THEME.md` / `AGENTS.md` / `.cursorrules`.

**Locked:** deml-ui owns the look; Viking is fully retired.
